   SigningBrokerError interpolation are unchanged. The rootless-broker case
   pins the exact resulting message.
4. Manifest key ID: The broker-root-derived key-ID comparison still happens
   before value parsing and receipt. An unknown key ID paired with an invalid
   value proves the unchanged unknown-key issue wins.
5. Value type/base64/length: Non-string, non-ASCII, invalid base64, and 63-byte
   decoded values all return the same invalid-signature issue before receipt.
6. Raw public key extraction: The new keyring needs raw bytes, but the same
   helper has already been invoked by the unchanged key-ID gate. A serialization
   failure is therefore not newly reachable after the gate.
7. Signed bytes/domain: The delegation test observes the exact payload,
   signature map, public-key map, keyring, domain, and label. It asserts the
   domain equals canonical_signing_message("apply_ed25519", b""); real round-trip
   and wrong-domain tests pin acceptance and domain separation.
8. Trust mechanics: The keyring fingerprint is computed from the already
   accepted protected broker root at call time. It adds shared mechanics and an
   N-of-M-ready shape, not a new trust anchor. Delegation and wrong-key tests pin
   this.
9. Cryptographic rejection: Old InvalidSignature became receipt SignError; both
   are converted to exactly "has an invalid encoder apply manifest signature".
   Flipped signature byte, one-byte payload mutation, wrong key, and wrong domain
   all exercise the real receipt implementation and pin that string.
10. Keyring/config SignError: Receipt can also use SignError for its own
    verification/keyring refusals. All keyring fields are fixed constants or
    derived from a validated Ed25519 root, so no additional supported-input
    refusal is reachable. If receipt nevertheless refuses, its internal message
    is not exposed; callers receive the existing invalid-signature issue.
11. Other receipt exceptions: Non-SignError programming/package faults are not
    swallowed. The exact version/hash pin and real-path tests protect the API.
    A completely missing package now produces the required eager ImportError.
12. Success and callers: Successful verification still returns None; all
    production callers and issue-string composition are unchanged. The existing
    tests/test_cli.py oracle remained unedited and passed.

